ng through a  dance of the fire god to sumiyoshi and  his descendants until he got to tanjiru  now tundra was not immediately as  talented as yorichi and his youth so  he's not the chosen one in the sense  that he's naturally the most talented  person ever but he is the chosen one in  the sense that with enough training and  help he was the one able to finally  finish off muzon using sun breathing  something that even yurichi didn't  succeed in doing tundra's chosen one  potential is made clear throughout the  series and he is consistently getting  stronger in accomplishing more and more  impressive feats he helps hashtag and  uzui beat upper moon 6 gyutaro after his  demonstrator mark evolves to look even  more like yorichi's proving once and for  all that it's not just a scar with this  evolved mark he actually manages to cut  the upper moon's neck something hasha  tangen couldn't even do when hashira  iguro shows up telling tengen not to  retire tengen says someone has grown  strong enough to help replace him  meaning tanjiro so even at this point  you could make the argument that tundra  deserves to be considered hashira level  especially with the dwindling number of  hashira and what's more tundra only gets  stronger from here with each fight he  starts to look more and more like  yorichi in one way or another against  kyotaro his scar temporarily changed to  look more like urichi's against upper  moon 4 he uses yorichi's own 300 year  old blade and turns it red when  delivering the final blow during the  tanjiro and giu vs akaza fight his  demonstrator mark extends again and he  gains access to the transparent world  another ability that odichi had in this  state he can easily avoid akka's final  form attack which even demon slayer mark  giu fails to do furthermore akaza  realizes tundra reached a selfless state  which is viewed as the domain of  supremacy for martial artists the thing  akasa has been aiming towards his whole  life this state is characterized 